    "description": "<div class=\"Box-sc-62in7e-0 js-snippet-clipboard-copy-unpositioned DirectoryRichtextContent-module__SharedMarkdownContent--BTKsc\">\n<h2>Dataset for the E-bike Demonstration Case</h2>\n<p>We create an electric bicycle (e-bike) architecture in a linear fashion using RFLP (Requirement - Functional - Logic - Physical) as an approach. It is essential to note that RFLP represents only one of many potential approaches for MBSE. &nbsp;We know that the RFLP process covers many different aspects and includes various application tools. Our example, therefore, only shows an overview and is created with Enterprise Architect and Solidworks. In the process, we use SysML, CAD volume modelling (tools), and the Finite Element Method (FEM).</p>\n<p>The dataset is created in the context of the paper <strong>Toward Demystifying the Missing Links in Model-Based Systems Engineering (MBSE)</strong> by Azad Khandoker, Sabine Sint, Guido Gessl and Klaus Zeman, currently under publication in the <a href=\"https://www.mdpi.com/journal/systems\">Journal Systems</a>.</p>\n<h3>Structure of the record</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>E-Bike_Architectures.eapx:<br>The e-bike model is an Enterprise Architect file, where user needs, requirements, functions and logic are represented.<br><br></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>functionalDesign.pdf, logicalArchitecture.pdf, physicalArchitecture.pdf, technicalRequirements.pdf, userNeeds.pdf:<br>Exported pdf files from the e-bike model<br><br></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>ebike-frame.SLDPRT:<br>The SolidWorks simulation file of the e-bike for the physical model<br><br></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>simulation.pdf:<br>Results of the simulation of the e-bike in SolidWorks.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3>Needed Software</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>pdf: pdf Viewer for the exported files from the different programs</li>\n<li>eapx: Enterprise Architect Version 16 (or newer) from Sparx Systems;&nbsp;<a href=\"https://sparxsystems.com/\">https://sparxsystems.com/</a></li>\n<li>sldprt: SolidWorks 2022 (or newer); <a href=\"https://www.solidworks.com/\">https://www.solidworks.com/</a></li>\n</ul>"
  },
